## 8. ANOMALY DETECTION FORMULA

The anomaly detection uses a dynamic threshold based on rolling statistics:

$$A(t) = \frac{\sum_{i=t-W}^{t} |a_i - \mu_W|}{\sqrt{\sum_{i=t-W}^{t} (a_i - \mu_W)^2}} \cdot \sigma_{\text{base}}$$

Where:
- $a_i$ = instantaneous acceleration magnitude
- $W$ = window size (60 samples)
- $\mu_W$ = rolling mean acceleration
- $\sigma_{\text{base}}$ = base standard deviation (calibrated to 0.85g)

When $A(t) > 3.0$, the system flags an anomaly.

